Lets the Bench2Drive leaderboard drive against a CARLA server started beforehand, on Python 3.9+. The evaluator no
longer launches its own server from CARLA_ROOT on a free port (nor kills it after a crash), connects to the client and
the traffic manager once and raises when either is unreachable instead of retrying for minutes, and reads weather.xml
next to the package instead of from the working directory. The route and scenario parsers drop
Element.getchildren(), which Python 3.9 removed. setup_carla.sh applies it.

